# ============================================================================
# Snakefile_dog: annotation comparison for the DOG study
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Study : Canine cryptorchidism / KAT6A (PNAS 2024, doi:10.1073/pnas.2312724121)
# Data  : the 22 libraries deposited in SRA PRJNA901164 (PE ~101 bp, TruSeq
#         Stranded mRNA, NovaSeq 6000), downloaded from ENA
# Alignment and counting:
#   STAR 2.5.3a, GENOME-ONLY index, splice junctions inserted at mapping time
#   from the GTF (--sjdbGTFfile, overhang 100), default STAR settings, untrimmed
#   reads; featureCounts paired, REVERSE-stranded (-s 2), -O -M.
# Every annotation is treated the same way, each on its OWN genome with native
# chromosome names (no renaming):
#   ensembl : Ensembl 92 genome + Ensembl 92 GTF + gene models for AMH and HMGA2,
#             which release 92 lacks (../../data/dog_added_gene_models/amh_hmga2.gtf)
#   refseq  : RefSeq GCF_000002285.3 genome + RefSeq GTF   (NC_... names)
#   ucsc    : UCSC canFam3 genome + canFam3.ncbiRefSeq GTF  (chr... names)
# Requires star_index_mode: per_annotation.
# Run   :  snakemake -s Snakefile_dog --profile profiles/slurm
# ============================================================================

